 league run, according to Bay Area News Group. ([chicoer.com](https://www.chicoer.com/2026/07/18/what-weve-learned-about-yaxel-lendeborg-from-warriors-summer-league/))

The early returns on the shooting question have been encouraging. Bay Area News Group reports Lendeborg made 15 of 31 three-point attempts across his Las Vegas games â€” an admittedly small sample, though one the coverage calls "whopping." His three-point rate had reached 37 percent in his final collegiate seasons at UAB, a number that existed in tension with the non-shooter reputation he carried through his earlier years, and observers are now watching to see whether that late improvement carries forward at the professional level. ([chicoer.com](https://www.chicoer.com/2026/07/18/what-weve-learned-about-yaxel-lendeborg-from-warriors-summer-league/))

The mechanics have drawn as much attention as the percentage. Bay Area News Group describes his shooting as compact and suited to catch-and-shoot work from the corners, with coverage raising questions about whether his role resembles that of a corner specialist like De'Anthony Melton. Lendeborg was also asked about his mechanics in the context of the Warriors' system, with Steph Curry raised in that discussion, per the same reporting. ([chicoer.com](https://www.chicoer.com/2026/07/18/what-weve-learned-about-yaxel-lendeborg-from-warriors-summer-league/))

Lendeborg's summer began in the California Classic before the Las Vegas bracket. Bay Area News Group puts his output across those two California games at 7 and 9 points, with the form looking sound. In Las Vegas the production expanded to 15 points in one game, alongside four blocks, three assists, and two rebounds, per the same reporting. ([chicoer.com](https://www.chicoer.com/2026/07/18/what-weve-learned-about-yaxel-lendeborg-from-warriors-summer-league/))

The Warriors went 3-1 as a team through the summer league bracket. Bay Area News Group reports the team beat the Los Angeles Lakers 92-88 to advance to the semifinals and defeated Memphis 106-85 in a Tuesday matchup. LJ Cryer was among the other contributors in the Warriors' summer rotation, per the coverage. ([chicoer.com](https://www.chicoer.com/2026/07/18/what-weve-learned-about-yaxel-lendeborg-from-warriors-summer-league/))

The context around Lendeborg's evaluation carries more weight than most summer league assessments. Bay Area News Group notes that large portions of Golden State's anticipated 2026-27 rotation are expected to miss time with injuries â€” Jimmy Butler's knee issue among them, and Moses Moody also expected to be unavailable for a stretch. Steve Kerr's team carries several unresolved questions about its present makeup and longer-term direction, and the summer league slate was framed in the coverage as a seven-game window for answering some of them. ([chicoer.com](https://www.chicoer.com/2026/07/18/what-weve-learned-about-yaxel-lendeborg-from-warriors-summer-league/))

Lendeborg addressed his aims in remarks to Bay Area broadcasters during the summer league. Per Bay Area News Group, he spoke about trying to bring his best and help make the team a winner. ([chicoer.com](https://www.chicoer.com/2026/07/18/what-weve-learned-about-yaxel-lendeborg-from-warriors-summer-league/))

Free agency extended into its fourth week as the summer league continued, leaving the Warriors' full roster picture unsettled and the scope of Lendeborg's eventual role uncertain. ([chicoer.com](https://www.chicoer.com/2026/07/18/what-weve-learned-about-yaxel-lendeborg-from-warriors-summer-league/))

Bay Area News Group treats summer league performance explicitly as an indication rather than a guarantee of readiness. The question the coverage holds open is whether the shooting numbers Lendeborg posted in Las Vegas reflect durable skill development or a limited-competition artifact â€” and whether the rotation opening that Golden State's injury situation may create gives him regular-season minutes to answer that definitively. ([chicoer.com](https://www.chicoer.com/2026/07/18/what-weve-learned-about-yaxel-lendeborg-from-warriors-summer-league/))ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;yaTS7CxrbM7NR8OTfXRvpecarhWq6EZeH7N0k9xvWMsƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkx9ni:///sha-256;0vByh4IEj3Ti1zycvT09Ed_cCF3LLClkqv-O398RENMƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;X2a5Xat5h7uf5B1klpr3dMHpz0X0I-n-WjyiTGV5Twwƒdpairƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmark`ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;TqqtJrFZihuD6V5myK2chcJ3jYFsmH0pBr7szyUHYKkƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkxclaude-code-cli-invocationsƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;sCqdwBiSdxet4hhMTphNQCK6TOFAivAxj-fiZ0IN4dwƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarka1ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;jBYOMRmuf3KfyALb30iIrsxSoTzA03eiSVgrN2JP6gcƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarkg314.976ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;zA5olvLvjen7VwEuWWOkZ3CPA25NzEZ7F-9szt-Kq0oƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarkefalseƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;A5tLp0milP58wsJmS48S0-GArsPwjBC1GpIShit5hTAƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit